// get_user_info.dg — live name/email lookup for a resolved actor id. Used to attribute
// compensation emails (see ../actions/send_compensation_emails.dg) to whoever is really acting,
// instead of a hardcoded name/address.
//
// zoho.crm.getRecordById("users", userId) returns a Map with a "users" key holding a one-entry
// List, the same wrapped shape as the bulk zoho.crm.getRecords("users", ...) call in
// get_user_id_by_email.dg — confirmed live (reading fields off the raw Map result was wrong; see
// ../shared/get_user_profile.dg for the same fix).
//
// TODO: confirm the exact field names ("full_name" vs "Full_Name" etc.) once tested against a
// live response.
//
// Returns a JSON-stringified Map ({name, email}) — Standalone category functions can only
// declare return type string (confirmed via a live deploy error on apply_supervision_decision.dg
// — "Invalid return Type Map. Category standalone returns string"); callers parse the result
// back with .toMap() immediately at the call site.

string standalone.getUserInfo(String userId)
{
	users = zoho.crm.getRecordById("users", userId);
	user = users.get("users").get(0);
	info = Map();
	info.put("name", user.get("full_name"));
	info.put("email", user.get("email"));
	return info.toString();
}
